Storage 
Storage serves a different purpose. An LLM system may need to store: 
 training datasets;  
 processed training data;  
 model files;  
 checkpoints created during training;  
 evaluation results;  
 logs;  
 application data;  
 and documents used by retrieval systems.

 memory and storage systems;  
 networking equipment;  
 electrical power systems;  
 cooling systems;  
 physical security;  
 monitoring and management systems;  
 and mechanisms for backup and redundancy.  
These components must work together. For example, adding more computing servers also 
increases electricity consumption and the amount of heat that must be removed. Increasing the 
number of servers may therefore require corresponding increases in power and cooling capacity. 
This illustrates an important principle: Computing capacity cannot be considered independently 
from the physical infrastructure required to support it. 
