Treat Prompt Engineering as a Communication Skill 
The practices discussed in this section can be summarized by viewing prompt engineering as a 
form of structured communication. An effective user communicates: 
 what should be accomplished;  
 what information is relevant;  
 what constraints must be respected;  
 what form the result should take;  
 and how the result will be evaluated.  
The user then examines the response and, when necessary, provides additional instructions.

