 and possible business rules implemented in the software.  
This can support reverse engineering and system modernization. For example, an analyst 
maintaining an old application might ask an LLM: "Which parts of this program determine 
whether a customer is eligible for a discount?" The LLM can examine the relevant source code 
and identify candidate logic for further investigation. 
Again, the result should be treated as an analysis aid rather than as authoritative documentation. 
