That is a much more difficult question. A model may be syntactically correct and visually 
convincing while still representing the wrong interpretation of the business problem. 
The systems analyst therefore remains responsible for determining: 
 whether the correct concepts have been identified;  
 whether relationships are represented correctly;  
 whether business rules have been captured;  
 whether the model is complete enough for its purpose;  
 and whether stakeholders agree with the interpretation.  
The LLM can significantly reduce the effort required to produce and manipulate models, but it 
does not eliminate the need for professional analysis.

