whether the result is appropriate. 
Design Validation 
A generated design must ultimately be validated. Validation may involve: 
 reviewing the architecture against requirements;  
 checking interfaces against actual system capabilities;  
 testing proposed database designs;  
 evaluating security;  
 building prototypes;  
 measuring performance;  
 and reviewing the design with users and technical specialists.

