Reverse Engineering and Legacy Systems 
This capability is particularly relevant to reverse engineering. Reverse engineering involves 
examining an existing system in order to understand its structure, behavior, and implementation. 
Organizations may need to reverse-engineer systems when: 
 documentation is missing;  
 the original development team is unavailable;  
 an old technology must be replaced;  
 the organization wants to migrate to a new platform;  
 or an existing application must be integrated with a new system.  
