The project manager should therefore consider the complete development process rather than 
assuming that faster generation automatically means faster project completion. 
New Skills for IS Professionals 
The growing use of LLMs may also change the skills expected from Information Systems 
professionals. Traditional technical and analytical skills remain important, but professionals may 
increasingly need to know how to: 
 formulate effective instructions;  
 provide appropriate context;  
 evaluate generated results;  
 recognize plausible but incorrect outputs;

