An LLM hallucination occurs when the model generates information that is inaccurate, 
unsupported, or fabricated while presenting it as though it were a meaningful response to the 
user's request. For example, an LLM might: 
 provide a non-existent reference;  
 attribute a statement to the wrong source;  
 invent details about a person or organization;  
 provide an incorrect explanation;  
 or generate a plausible but unsupported answer to a question.  
