A simple conceptual risk model is: Risk ≈ Likelihood × Impact 
This is not a precise mathematical formula. It is a way of emphasizing that both factors matter. 
For example, an occasional incorrect answer in a low-risk internal writing application may have 
limited consequences. An incorrect recommendation in an application supporting a high-impact 
decision may have much greater consequences even if the probability of the error is low. 
