Reducing Risk Rather Than Expecting Perfection 
It is generally unrealistic to expect an LLM-based system to be completely free of errors or 
security threats. The objective of risk management is therefore not necessarily to eliminate every 
possible risk. Instead, the organization should seek to reduce important risks to an acceptable 
level.

 proceed with deployment;  
 modify the system;  
 introduce additional controls;  
 restrict the system to particular uses;  
 require additional human oversight;  
 or decide not to deploy the system.  
This decision should be based on the particular application rather than on the capabilities of the 
LLM alone. 
Monitoring After Deployment 
Risk management does not end when the system is deployed. The organization should monitor 
whether: 
 new failure modes appear;  
 users employ the system in unexpected ways;  
 the underlying information changes;  
 security incidents occur;  
 the model or service changes;  
 or existing controls become inadequate.  
